      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Classes, Structs and Construction",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. class vs struct",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Default",
                "class",
                "struct"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Member access",
                  "{red:private}",
                  "{green:public}"
                ],
                [
                  "Inheritance",
                  "{red:private}",
                  "{green:public}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "That is the ==only difference==",
                "Constructors: ==no return type==, run **once per object**",
                "Compiler adds a ==default constructor== only if you declare **no** constructor"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Initializer list",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct Foo {",
                "  int x, y;",
                "  Foo(int a) : x(a), y(a * 2) {}",
                "  Foo() : Foo(0) {}  // delegating",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "list runs before the body"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Required== for `const` members, reference members, members with no default constructor",
                "Members init in ==declaration order==, not list order",
                "Reordering the list changes nothing; `-Wreorder` warns when one member uses another"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. explicit",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Mark one-argument constructors ==explicit==",
                "Blocks implicit conversion: `Foo f = 5;` fails to compile",
                "Delegating constructor `Foo(): Foo(0) {}` reuses one constructor"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Init order",
              "text": "Declaration order decides, never the initializer list."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Destructors and the Rule of Three, Five and Zero",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Destructors and the Rule of Three, Five and Zero",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Destructor and Rule of Three",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`~Foo()` runs at ==scope exit== or `delete`",
                "Members destroyed in {blue:reverse declaration order}, then bases",
                "Custom destructor, copy ctor or copy assign: you need ==all three==",
                "Shallow copy of a raw pointer causes **double delete**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Five and Zero",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Rule",
                "You write"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Three",
                  "destructor, copy ctor, copy assign"
                ],
                [
                  "Five",
                  "+ `Foo(Foo&&) noexcept`, move assign"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Zero}",
                  "==nothing==: hold `unique_ptr`, `vector`, `string`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`noexcept` moves let `std::vector` ==move on growth==, not copy",
                "Rule of zero: compiler-generated ones are correct"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Assignment and defaults",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Copy assign must survive ==self-assignment== (`a = a`)",
                "Copy-and-swap gives that plus **exception safety**",
                "`=default` keeps a special member, `=delete` removes it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "Foo& operator=(Foo other) {",
                "    swap(*this, other);",
                "    return *this;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "by-value parameter is the copy"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Need one of the three? Write all five. Better: ==rule of zero==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Inheritance and Virtual Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Inheritance and Virtual Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Is-a and Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Public inheritance models ==is-a==",
                "`Derived(): Base(args) {}` runs the **base ctor first**",
                "Destruction runs in ==reverse== order"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Binding and the vtable",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "No virtual",
                "virtual"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Binds",
                  "compile time",
                  "run time"
                ],
                [
                  "Decided by",
                  "pointer's {blue:static} type",
                  "object's {green:dynamic} type"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One ==vtable== per class with virtuals: function pointers",
                "Each object has a hidden ==vptr==: one pointer of size",
                "Each virtual call costs **one indirect call**",
                "`override` turns a signature mismatch into a compile error",
                "`final` blocks further overriding or inheriting"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct B { virtual void f() const; virtual ~B() = default; };",
                "struct D : B { void f() const override; };",
                "struct E final : D {};"
              ],
              "note": "override on every override"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slicing: `Base b = derived;` copies only the Base part, no polymorphism",
                "Fix: pass `Base&` or `Base*`",
                "Virtual call in ctor or dtor resolves to the ==current class=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Polymorphism needs ==virtual== plus a **reference or pointer**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Abstract Classes and Virtual Destructors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Abstract Classes and Virtual Destructors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pure Virtual = Abstract",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`virtual void draw() const = 0;` makes the class ==abstract==",
                "Cannot be instantiated; use it only through {blue:pointers or references}",
                "A derived class stays abstract until it overrides ==every== pure virtual",
                "A pure virtual may still have a body, called as `Base::draw()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct Shape {",
                "  virtual ~Shape() = default;",
                "  virtual double area() const = 0;",
                "};",
                "std::vector<std::unique_ptr<Shape>> shapes;",
                "for (auto& s : shapes) s->area();"
              ],
              "note": "interface held by unique_ptr: runtime polymorphism"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Virtual Destructors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A base with virtual functions needs `virtual ~Base()`",
                "Non-virtual dtor + `delete` via `Base*` = {red:undefined behavior}, skips ~Derived",
                "A pure virtual destructor ==must be defined=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct Base { virtual ~Base() = 0; };",
                "Base::~Base() {}  // body is required"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interface recipe",
              "text": "`virtual ~X() = default;` plus pure virtuals, and own objects with `unique_ptr<X>`."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why a virtual destructor?** `delete` through `Base*` then runs ~Derived too",
                "**Pure virtual destructor with no body?** Linker error: ~Derived calls it",
                "**Is a class with a pure virtual body abstract?** Yes, still not instantiable"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Operator Overloading",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Operator Overloading",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "An operator is a function named ==operator+==, etc.",
                "No new operators; precedence is fixed",
                "Not overloadable: `::` `.` `.*` `?:` `sizeof`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Member or Free?",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Operators"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Member** (required)",
                  "`=` `[]` `()` `->`"
                ],
                [
                  "**Free** (symmetric)",
                  "`a + b`, `a == b`, `<<`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Free lets ==implicit conversion== work on the left operand"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Patterns",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "Foo& Foo::operator+=(const Foo& b) { x += b.x; return *this; }",
                "Foo operator+(Foo a, const Foo& b) { return a += b; }",
                "std::ostream& operator<<(std::ostream& os, const Foo& f) { return os << f.x; }",
                "auto operator<=>(const Foo&) const = default;",
                "Foo& operator++();   // prefix",
                "Foo operator++(int); // postfix"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Write `+=` first, build `+` on it",
                "`<<` is free (often `friend`), returns the stream",
                "`<=>` default gives all ==six== comparisons",
                "Postfix returns the old copy: {red:slower}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Mark non-modifying methods ==const== so they work on const objects."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
